KelpServer (crates/server, crates/protocol) was extracted from Kelpmux at
commit eb31da5 into the KelpServer repository, later renamed KelpCore
(https://github.com/joanfabregat/kelpcore). The client core (crates/client)
and the browser terminal layer (web-core/) were moved there from Kelpmux at
commit 7179aa3. KelpCore was merged back into Kelpmux with its history. All
of it remains the work of Joan Fabregat and the Kelpmux contributors, under
the same Apache-2.0 license.

The file operations (crates/server/src/native/files.rs) adapt the design and
parts of the code of KelpHub's workspace file browser
(server/src/management/files.rs at commit ed69304), Copyright 2026 Joan
Fabregat, moved into KelpCore under the Apache License, Version 2.0, with
the copyright holder's approval.

The file browser and editor UI (web-core/src/files/: the request client, path
and document models, language detection, the CodeMirror editor and its
theme) is derived from KelpHub (web/src/files/ at commit 7057705),
Copyright 2026 Joan Fabregat, moved with the copyright holder's approval
into KelpCore under the Apache License, Version 2.0.

Native release archives use Alacritty's terminal engine and other Rust
dependencies, copyright their respective authors. Exact versions, license
expressions and upstream license texts are included under dependency-licenses/.
Kelpmux's Apache-2.0 license does not replace those dependencies' licenses.

Native status-bar metrics incorporate code adapted from Vitals
(https://github.com/joanfabregat/vitals), Copyright (c) 2026 Joan Fabrégat,
licensed under MIT. The complete license is in assets/licenses/vitals-MIT.txt.

Optional embedded web assets include React and React DOM (MIT), the
CodeMirror 6 and Lezer packages of the file editor (MIT), Chromium
libapps WASSH/WASI bindings (BSD), and the upstream OpenSSH WASM client.
Browser-side OpenSSH incorporates OpenSSL, zlib and ldns. The web client also
bundles JetBrains Mono (SIL OFL 1.1), Lucide icon geometry (ISC) and terminal
palettes from Rootshell (MIT) and the upstream schemes listed in
web/THIRD_PARTY.md. Their separate license texts are embedded in the web
assets under /licenses/ and remain applicable independently of Kelpmux's
Apache-2.0 license.

